      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-05-01_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>CALEDONIAN ASSOCIATION—Continued</head>
        <p>CALEDONIAN ASSOCIATION—Continued</p>
        <p>taming the names of the members of the Association who had served or are. serving the King, was exhibited, and was greatly admired. In the corners are the words "Honour," "Justice," "Truth," "Liberty." • At the top centre is R representation of the flags of the Allies and the Scottish ' standard, with the words "Aye, ready for. right." At the bottom centre are drawn the shamrock, thistle and rose, with the injunction "Touch us gin ye &amp;lux." The "roll," so far, contains the follow- ing names:—</p>
